{
  "schema": "outcome.geo-vectors.v1",
  "description": "Portable conformance vectors for the RFC-005 integer geo semantics (scripts/lib/geo.mjs is the reference implementation; run by service/test/geo.test.mjs). Coordinates are [lonMicro, latMicro] integer micro-degrees; boundaries are canonical MultiPolygon coordinate arrays (closed rings, exterior CCW, holes CW, antimeridian pre-split). Expected values are NORMATIVE goldens: an implementation disagreeing with any vector does not implement the spec. relation semantics: on any ring edge or vertex = 'boundary' (within); strictly inside exterior and not strictly inside a hole = 'interior' (within); else 'outside'. polygon = index of first containing polygon in document order, -1 outside. Radius: equirectangular on R=6371000 m, Q31 fixed point (PI_Q31=6746518852, K_Q31=238789287), cos at the CENTER latitude via the pinned Taylor-Q31 algorithm, squared-distance compare, on-circle within; distanceMeters = floor meters.",
  "boundaries": {
    "convex-square": [[[[0, 0], [10000, 0], [10000, 10000], [0, 10000], [0, 0]]]],
    "concave-L": [[[[0, 0], [30000, 0], [30000, 10000], [10000, 10000], [10000, 30000], [0, 30000], [0, 0]]]],
    "square-with-hole": [[[[0, 0], [40000, 0], [40000, 40000], [0, 40000], [0, 0]], [[10000, 10000], [10000, 30000], [30000, 30000], [30000, 10000], [10000, 10000]]]],
    "antimeridian-split": [
